<title>GERMANY: Dutch prime minister Kok to visit Kohl in Bonn.</title>
<headline>Dutch prime minister Kok to visit Kohl in Bonn.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Prime Minister Wim Kok, who holds the rotating European Union presidency, will meet German Chancellor Helmut Kohl in Bonn on Wednesday amid turmoil over preparations for monetary union in 1999.</p>
<p>Kok has been visiting many European capitals this week in advance of next week's EU summit in Amsterdam.</p>
<p>In a brief statement, the German government said Kok and Kohl would meet at the chancellery at 5 p.m. (1500 GMT), where they would give brief statements.</p>
<p>The two leaders will be accompanied by their respective foreign ministers -- Hans van Mierlo and Klaus Kinkel.</p>
<p>No further information about the meeting was given.</p>
</text>
